config MESHTASTIC_KEYVERIFY
	bool "Meshtastic manual key verification (security-number handshake)"
	default y
	depends on MESHTASTIC_PKI && MESHTASTIC_NODEDB
	help
	  The reference KeyVerificationModule: a two-party handshake on
	  KEY_VERIFICATION_APP (port 12) that lets a user confirm, out of band,
	  that a peer holds the private key for the public key we have for it --
	  MitM-resistant -- and, in the bootstrap case, learn a peer's key from
	  the handshake itself. Driven from the app over AdminMessage
	  key_verification (INITIATE / PROVIDE_SECURITY_NUMBER / DO_VERIFY /
	  DO_NOT_VERIFY) or from the shell; prompts reach the app as
	  ClientNotification (number to show, number to enter, final code).
	  On accept the peer's key is committed to the NodeDB with the
	  "key manually verified" flag, which persists.
